  "worked_solution": "The total charge $Q$ of a plate that occupies the region $D$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y)=x$ is given by\n\n$$\nQ={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nLet's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066271/assets/2b179e35ae9af5a13d43c9a64bee99ee4ed87c257b623184f9165e14c24f3dee.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region. So, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{x}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{x}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}[y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{x}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}\u20610] \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total charge of the plate is $Q=1.$",
